BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 308.75 Tm (procedural, not budgetary: record every call, honoring two-party consent where it applies, and check intake before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 293.52 Tm (spending another dollar on marketing [lW3uPdauQrA @ 00:29:07].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 278.30 Tm (The phone itself is where leads bleed out. Alert Communications measured abandonment rising after three rings and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 263.07 Tm (again after a 15-second hold, and reported one firm running six-minute holds [PJEVefyQCxA @ 00:19:14]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 247.85 Tm (overflow sequence Alert prescribes is three rings, a recorded message, a 15-second hold, then roll to the overflow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 232.62 Tm (center [PJEVefyQCxA @ 00:21:02]. Alert also found voicemail or no answer on 35% of calls, and flags paralegals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 217.40 Tm (juggling intake alongside other work as a weak point [PJEVefyQCxA @ 00:28:06]. Repeat-attempt data shows why) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 202.17 Tm (one dial is never enough: immediate calls reach 37% to 40%, and varying call times lifts contact to 75% to 80%) Tj ET
