BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 692.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 669.77 Tm (The first trap is the cash hole that opens before a single dollar comes back. Casey Gard walks through the arithmetic:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 654.55 Tm (500 cases at $10,000 each means $5 million laid out up front, and Dodd-Frank-era limits keep banks from lending) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.32 Tm (against contingency assets, which is why firms land at funders' doors [g66VtR5b5gQ @ 00:22:25]. Ted Farrell itemizes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.10 Tm (the hard costs behind that number, with $400 to $500 filing fees, medical record orders, and nurse review pushing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 608.87 Tm (workup into the thousands per case, so that 10,000 clients at $3,000 each becomes roughly $30 million) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 593.65 Tm ([gdDT2WSKYs0 @ 00:10:38]. Farrell mocks the advertising pitch directly: "at 3,000 bucks a pop you know just come) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.42 Tm (up with 15 million bucks and you too could you know be doing those cases" [gdDT2WSKYs0 @ 00:09:21]. Dave) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.20 Tm (Kirsty names the two internal gaps that turn that burn into a crisis: poor budgeting and no partner-compensation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 547.97 Tm (mechanism for cases carried on risk, a problem that bites because funders cap their commitment at 50 to 70 percent of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 532.75 Tm (the budget [fTOe5KR6QSE @ 00:14:45]. Camp Lejeune adds a timing drag on top, since every claim requires an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 517.52 Tm (individual administrative process before filing, stretching the period in which cash is out and nothing is returning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.30 Tm (Valuation errors are the second recurring loss. Adam Rosen of Rocade, an ex-Ashcraft & Gerel MDL litigator, warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.07 Tm (that naive per-plaintiff averaging overvalues "product in place" dockets, and the firms that lean on it keep refinancing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 471.85 Tm (instead of getting paid [Zz1HlCrfQPY @ 00:52:13]. Rocade's fix is to value every case by injury subtype rather than a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 456.62 Tm (settlement average, which is how the shop modeled three separate 3M grids in 2020, and Rosen's blunt summary is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.40 Tm ("Data is everything," meaning fee splits, expenses and surgery dates tracked well beyond intake [Zz1HlCrfQPY @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.17 Tm (00:28:47]. TownCenter Partners breaks personal-injury value into damages, liability and insurance, noting that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 410.95 Tm (damages only come clear after maximum medical improvement and that liability is the hardest piece to calculate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 395.72 Tm ([1Xs5nnkcuL4 @ 00:01:35]. Dave Kirsty adds the final check: winning is not the same as collecting, and firms must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 380.50 Tm (build their case math around collectability, with case value sitting at roughly 10x the commitment so the waterfall still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.27 Tm (works after the funder's multiple [fTOe5KR6QSE @ 00:15:42]. A docket that looks rich on averages, unvalidated by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.05 Tm (subtype, MMI status and collection prospects, is the docket that ends in a refinancing loop rather than a payout.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.82 Tm (The third category is counterparty and rule-change risk that firms rarely see coming. Ted Farrell warns that some) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 319.60 Tm (funders are past their fund's investment period and will not admit it, which is why advisers time approaches for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.37 Tm (moments such as right after a "fund two" closes [gdDT2WSKYs0 @ 00:18:57]. Farrell also flags odd clauses buried in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.15 Tm (documents that have no standard form, including attorney-in-fact rights triggered on a "material risk of a bankruptcy") Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 273.92 Tm ([gdDT2WSKYs0 @ 00:20:13]. Adam Rosen tells firms to hire transactional counsel and to raise capital only when) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 258.70 Tm (reinvestment returns beat its cost, and saves the harshest warning for MSO deals: "You're trading away a ton of upsides) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 243.47 Tm (for a little upfront cash," with California cited as a regulatory wipeout risk for those structures [Zz1HlCrfQPY @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.25 Tm (01:24:31]. Rosen also notes that North Carolina's ban blocks some appeal deals outright, so jurisdiction decides which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.02 Tm (products are even available. Oregon Law Lab adds that a change in law or treaty mid-case can make an investment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 197.80 Tm (worthless "or even negative," the flip side of the hedge-fund pitch that litigation holds value whether the market goes) Tj ET
