BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.77 Tm (The ABS failures already on the record cluster around firms that forgot they are law firms. Lynda Shely reports that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.55 Tm (two compliance lawyers have been disciplined and reads that as proof the system works, but the operator takeaway is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.32 Tm (that the named ethics officer is the first person exposed when a firm slips [OdPOa3osKC0 @ 00:10:44]. Shely also) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 496.10 Tm (warns against the cheap compliance-lawyer model: the role needs management experience, and one person should not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.87 Tm (be stretched across five to seven firms [OdPOa3osKC0 @ 00:19:39]. The sharpest trap hits mass-tort and PI operators,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.65 Tm (who made up 26 of the 65 ABS firms counted in the three-year update: a bar complaint is pending over a firm allegedly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.42 Tm (just referring cases out, and Shely states an Arizona lawyer must give substantive input on intake, medical-record) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 435.20 Tm (review and client communication, so an empty Arizona office funneling cases to Florida is not allowed [poe1CAsUc4U) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.97 Tm (@ 00:36:28]. On the Law Leaders update, Shely closes with the line every tort aggregator should keep in view: this is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.75 Tm (not a get-rich-quick scheme, even though ER 7.2's elimination now lets Arizona lawyers pay non-lawyers referral fees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.52 Tm (as a percentage of fees, with no bar charges so far [Tvn12qG9i5s @ 00:27:40].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.30 Tm (On the healthcare side, the failures that blow up MSO structures are mundane and operational. Holt Law's warning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 359.07 Tm (example is a clinic posting before-and-after photos without patient consent and running QuickBooks payroll that was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.85 Tm (misfiled with missed taxes, exactly the back-office work an MSO is supposed to absorb [bXO6V29iXPs @ 00:03:37].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.62 Tm (The structural leak Holt Law flags is owners pushing clinical assets such as lasers over to the MSO side, when a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.40 Tm (conservative read keeps Botox, filler, clinical salaries and even medical equipment inside the clinical entity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 298.17 Tm ([Oa-6OBD0Gak @ 00:04:04]. Erin Jackson cautions that an MSO is never a single filing: it needs additional contracts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.95 Tm (and a medical director to keep non-physician operators clear of the practice of medicine, and the private-equity exit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.72 Tm (story carries no guarantees on what PE may be interested in [4niOtoceEKc @ 00:01:15]. CorporateAttorneysCA lists) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.50 Tm (the downstream penalty stack: regulatory issues can arise around the corporate practice of medicine, fee splitting and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.27 Tm (the Stark law, which can result in serious consequences if violated [cTWDG8n6ks0 @ 00:01:56]. The economics check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 222.05 Tm (is simple: if the MSA, the asset split and the medical director are not airtight, the efficiency pitch becomes the liability.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.82 Tm (Deal-side traps hit before and after closing. Frederick Shelton warns that some investment bankers overpromise 10x) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.60 Tm (multiples to collect $1 million to $2 million success fees, while an actual offer of 4x profit compares poorly with the 6x) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.37 Tm (to 8x Shelton sees in the market, and closing before January can hand 30% to 40% to taxes [I4F5OYZQJuU @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 161.15 Tm (00:24:08]. Shelton's governance kill-switch is a board with one attorney facing four PE directors who control) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.92 Tm (equity-partner decisions, which Shelton labels controlling the practice of law [I4F5OYZQJuU @ 00:31:10]. Holt Law) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.70 Tm (adds two post-close risks: investor pressure on the firm, and the fact that lawyers often cannot be bound by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.47 Tm (non-competes, so the only shield is an ironclad MSA [DNk78wbKy5s @ 00:05:58]. Kvesic frames the traditional) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.25 Tm (partnership as its own failure mode: partners sweep cash to zero in December, run on a January credit line, and resume) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 85.02 Tm (draws in March or April, which Kvesic calls a ridiculous way to run a business, while a bank loan simply adds a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 69.80 Tm (creditor with liens on receivables [_P68fUIZN48 @ 00:24:17]. Before signing, operators should price the multiple, the) Tj ET
